---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Dynamic Building Risk Analysis | Amirhossein Eskorouchi"
  description="An interactive Streamlit dashboard for scenario-based multi-hazard building risk screening and discounted cumulative risk analysis."
>
  <article class="project-page">
    <header class="project-header">
      <p class="project-kicker">
        Decision Support &middot; Risk Analysis &middot; Geospatial Visualization
      </p>

      <h1>Dynamic Building Risk Analysis</h1>

      <p class="project-summary">
        A configurable dashboard for exploring how building characteristics,
        hazard scenarios, annual probabilities, and financial assumptions
        influence scenario-based risk estimates.
      </p>

      <p class="project-links">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/amirhossein-eskorouchi/Dynamic-Building-Risk-Analysis"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          View code
        </a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="project-hero-figure">
      <a
        href="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/dashboard-overview.png"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
        aria-label="Open the full-resolution Dynamic Building Risk dashboard"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/dashboard-overview.png"
          alt="Full Dynamic Building Risk Assessment dashboard showing configuration controls, hazard scenarios, financial metrics, a satellite map, and ranked cumulative risk"
          width="2047"
          height="1017"
        />
      </a>

      <figcaption>
        The complete assessment workspace combines scenario configuration,
        summary metrics, geospatial context, risk ranking, and detailed results.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Project purpose</h2>

      <p>
        Building-risk decisions often require users to consider several hazard
        types, physical characteristics, location information, and long-term
        financial effects together. This project demonstrates how those inputs
        can be organized into one interactive screening workflow.
      </p>

      <p>
        The application was developed as an early Ph.D. proof of concept and
        later refreshed for reliable demonstration and portfolio presentation.
        The original scenario assumptions and calculation structure were
        preserved while the interface, mapping workflow, visual hierarchy, and
        reproducibility documentation were improved.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Assessment workflow</h2>

      <div class="project-fact-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Building profile</h3>
          <p>
            Users configure occupancy, construction type, building size,
            elevation, and proximity to the hazard source.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Hazard scenarios</h3>
          <p>
            The assessment supports hurricanes, storm surge, rainfall,
            earthquakes, floods, windstorms, snow and ice, landslides, and
            fire hazards.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Financial horizon</h3>
          <p>
            A discount rate and planning period convert expected annual risk
            into discounted cumulative exposure.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Geospatial context</h3>
          <p>
            Satellite and OpenStreetMap basemaps show the assessment location,
            with an optional MapLibre-based 3D view.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Scenario configuration</h2>

      <figure class="project-wide-figure">
        <a
          href="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/hazard-scenarios.png"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          aria-label="Open the full-resolution hazard-scenario configuration"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/hazard-scenarios.png"
            alt="Hazard configuration interface with selected natural hazards and scenario severity controls"
            width="1851"
            height="660"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>

        <figcaption>
          Users select the hazards included in the assessment and assign one
          probability-and-severity scenario to each selected hazard.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Risk calculations</h2>

      <div class="calculation-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="calculation-label">Expected annual risk</p>
          <p class="calculation-expression">
            Annual risk = scenario probability &times; potential damage
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="calculation-label">Discounted cumulative risk</p>
          <p class="calculation-expression">
            NPV = sum of annual risk / (1 + discount rate)<sup>t</sup>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Potential damage begins with an occupancy- and severity-specific base
        value. The application then applies multipliers for building size,
        construction type, elevation, proximity, and the selected hazard type.
        Results are calculated independently for every selected scenario and
        aggregated for dashboard reporting.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Spatial and financial interpretation</h2>

      <div class="project-media-grid">
        <figure>
          <a
            href="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/satellite-location.png"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            aria-label="Open the full-resolution assessment-location map"
          >
            <img
              src="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/satellite-location.png"
              alt="Satellite map showing the selected building assessment location"
              width="958"
              height="646"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </a>

          <figcaption>
            The selected coordinates provide geographic context for the
            assessment rather than automatically determining hazard exposure.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <a
            href="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/risk-concentration.png"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            aria-label="Open the full-resolution hazard-risk ranking"
          >
            <img
              src="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/risk-concentration.png"
              alt="Horizontal bar chart ranking selected hazards by discounted cumulative risk"
              width="814"
              height="463"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </a>

          <figcaption>
            Hazard ranking reveals which selected scenario contributes most
            strongly to cumulative risk under the configured assumptions.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Detailed hazard breakdown</h2>

      <figure class="project-wide-figure">
        <a
          href="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/hazard-breakdown.png"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          aria-label="Open the full-resolution hazard results table"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/projects/dynamic-building-risk-analysis/hazard-breakdown.png"
            alt="Detailed results table containing hazard, scenario, severity, annual probability, potential damage, annual risk, and cumulative net present value"
            width="1828"
            height="466"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>

        <figcaption>
          The results table preserves the full calculation trail for each
          selected hazard, including probability, damage, annual risk, and
          discounted cumulative risk.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Technical implementation</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Streamlit provides the interactive building, hazard, financial, and
          location controls.
        </li>
        <li>
          Pandas structures the scenario results and prepares the detailed
          assessment table.
        </li>
        <li>
          Matplotlib creates the ranked cumulative-risk visualization.
        </li>
        <li>
          Folium and Streamlit-Folium provide satellite and OpenStreetMap views.
        </li>
        <li>
          LeafMap and MapLibre support an optional API-key-enabled 3D basemap.
        </li>
        <li>
          Session state preserves the latest completed assessment while users
          inspect the resulting dashboard.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section">
      <h2>Illustrative dashboard result</h2>

      <p>
        In the configuration shown above, seven hazards produce approximately
        $2.92 million in combined potential damage, $0.066 million in expected
        annual risk, and $1.69 million in discounted cumulative risk over the
        selected horizon. Hurricane and high-wind exposure is the largest
        contributor in this illustrative scenario.
      </p>

      <p>
        These values demonstrate the application's calculation and
        visualization workflow. They are not general conclusions about the
        mapped location or any real building.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-section project-note">
      <h2>Responsible interpretation</h2>

      <p>
        This application is a scenario-based educational prototype. Its
        probabilities, base damage values, multipliers, and hazard
        relationships are project assumptions rather than calibrated,
        site-specific engineering estimates. The map provides location context
        but does not retrieve authoritative hazard data for the selected
        coordinates.
      </p>

      <p>
        The results should not be used for structural safety, insurance,
        emergency management, investment, or other real-world risk decisions.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .project-page {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .project-header {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .project-kicker {
    color: var(--muted, #536174);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .project-header h1 {
    max-width: 60rem;
  }

  .project-summary {
    max-width: 58rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .project-links {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .project-hero-figure,
  .project-wide-figure,
  .project-media-grid figure {
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
  }

  .project-hero-figure {
    max-width: 76rem;
    margin: 2rem auto 3rem;
  }

  .project-wide-figure {
    max-width: 74rem;
  }

  .project-hero-figure img,
  .project-wide-figure img,
  .project-media-grid img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border, #dfe5ec);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--muted, #536174);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .project-detail-section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .project-detail-section > p,
  .project-detail-section > ul {
    max-width: 70rem;
  }

  .project-detail-section li + li {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
  }

  .project-fact-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .project-fact-grid > div {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border, #dfe5ec);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  .project-fact-grid h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
  }

  .project-fact-grid p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .calculation-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 70rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .calculation-grid > div {
    background: var(--surface, #f5f8fb);
    border: 1px solid var(--border, #dfe5ec);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
  }

  .calculation-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted, #536174);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .calculation-expression {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .project-media-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .project-media-grid figure {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .project-note {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border, #dfe5ec);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .project-fact-grid,
    .calculation-grid,
    .project-media-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .project-detail-section {
      margin-top: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>